                        "content": "A client arrives in the hospital emergency department with a closed head injury to the right side of the head caused by an assault with a baseball bat. The nurse assesses the client neurologically, looking primarily for motor response deficits that involve which area?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nMotor responses such as weakness and decreased movement will be seen on the side of the body that is opposite an area of head injury. Contralateral deficits result from compression of the cortex of the brain or the pyramidal tracts. Depending on the severity of the injury, the client may have a variety of neurological deficits.",
                        "id": "2288f9c0c5ce43ba807e0a18f11a210f",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "439bc3ba2c484f30bb18a1d30827cb1f",
                                "content": "Sternal rub"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "0977c31a0a534632bad3399e1dcba339",
                                "content": "Pressure on nail beds"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "ba1c81118a764cba879f067b880057c2",
                                "content": "Pressure on the orbital rim"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "d5e102a4e9304e61a199a713d5d2290d",
                                "content": "Squeezing of the sternocleidomastoid muscle"
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "439bc3ba2c484f30bb18a1d30827cb1f",
                                    "content": "Sternal rub"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "1",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "0977c31a0a534632bad3399e1dcba339",
                                    "content": "Pressure on nail beds"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "ba1c81118a764cba879f067b880057c2",
                                    "content": "Pressure on the orbital rim"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "d5e102a4e9304e61a199a713d5d2290d",
                                    "content": "Squeezing of the sternocleidomastoid muscle"
                                }
                            ]
