                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nA change in vital signs may be a late sign of increased intracranial pressure. Trends include increasing temperature, widening pulse pressure, increased systolic blood pressure, and decreasing pulse and respirations. Respiratory irregularities also may occur.",
