                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nThe goal is to maintain the partial pressure of arterial carbon dioxide (PaCo2) at 35 to 38 mm Hg. Carbon dioxide is a very potent vasodilator that can contribute to increases in ICP. The Pao2 is not allowed to fall below 80 mm Hg, to prevent cerebral vasodilation from hypoxemia, which can also result in an increase in ICP. Therefore, the remaining options are incorrect.",
